Image SXM history        v1.58        ( Jul 95 - Dec 95 )____________________________________________________________________________________v1.58    ∑6    ( 3 Dec 95 )Added features:	•	A number of changes have been made to the 3d Plot dialog box. New options: (i) a 2d Plot option, producing a conventional flat image, may be useful for mixing the image colours with shadows to obtain a better impression of the surface topography; (ii) a 4d Plot option produces a 3d plot of an image with the colours of each pixel in the image tinted according to whether or not the corresponding pixel of a second image (which is assumed to have been density sliced previously) lies between the slice limits set. Selecting '3d Plot' with the Option key pressed now produces a smaller (faster) preview on 68K Macs and a larger (more detailed) preview on PowerMacs.Bug fixes:	•	Some items in the ReCalibrate XY dialog box were inadvertently disabled in ∑5, resulting in miscalibration of images. These items have been enabled again.Other changes:	•	A number of changes have been made to the STM Options dialog box. A popup menu has been added to allow the user to select options specific to the SPM that they use. If an SPM manufacturer is selected, the dialog box expands downwards to show any additional options. The options for XY tilt compensation or quadratic background subtraction have been simplified. Balloon Help has been added for the items in this dialog box.	•	There are now separate XY calibration files for Omicron, Burleigh, WA Technology, Digital, TopoMetrix and Park Scientific SPMs. Thus, calibration of an SPM image from one manufacturer does not affect the calibration of images from other manufacturers.  •  The 'ReCalibrate XY' command now works for images that are initially uncalibrated, such as PICT or TIFF images produced by other applications.  •  The continuous display of XYZ data in the Info window for FFT images now displays XY position (in pixels) and the frequency and period corresponding to that position.   •  The 'Resize Window' submenu has been moved from the SXM menu into the Windows menu. The keyboard shortcut cmd-1 has been added for the 100% setting.  •  The keyboard shortcut for 'Measure' in the Analyze menu has changed to cmd-M (previously cmd-1).  •  The 'Browse Images...' menu item has been removed from the SXM menu. This was functionally identical to the same menu item in the SEM and STM menus.____________________________________________________________________________________v1.58    ∑5    ( 5 Nov 95 )Added features:	•	Image SXM can now read HDF (Hierarchical Data Format) image files produced by the Park Scientific Instruments SPM. This has been tested on only a limited number of images.	•	A new 'Unsharp Mask' item has been added to the Process menu. It executes a convolution with a 15 x 15 Gaussian kernel, subtracts the result from the original image and then enhances the contrast. This command can be used to remove large-scale variations in intensity from an image to reveal smaller-scale detail.	•	A new option has been added to the STM Options dialog box. As an alternative to X and Y tilt compensation, a bi-quadratic background can be subtracted from an image during loading. This option was requested by an Image SXM user.	•	A new option has been added to the 3d Plot dialog box. The original image LUT colours and the shadows calculated from the illumination of the surface can be mixed together. This option was requested by an Image SXM user. Bug fixes:	•	Digital Instruments Nanoscope images did not display the correct Z scale. This has been fixed.Other changes:	•	Image SXM has been recompiled using CodeWarrior release 7.	•	When changing file types and creators, the dialog box now shows all files in the folder selected regardless of their type. Files of type 'APPL' and text files with filenames ending in '.PAR' or '.par' will not be altered.	•	The 'Resize Window' submenu has been extended to 400%. Keyboard shortcuts cmd-2 and cmd-4 have been added for 200% and 400% enlargement, respectively.____________________________________________________________________________________v1.58    ∑4    ( 1 Oct 95 )Added features:	•	None. Bug fixes:	•	The FPU and noFPU versions of Image SXM ∑3 crashed on startup due to a compilation error. The PowerMac version appears to be OK. All versions have been recompiled.Other changes:	•	Minor changes to 3d Plot dialog box.____________________________________________________________________________________v1.58    ∑3    ( 26 Sep 95 )Added features:	•	Image SXM can now read image files produced by the Digital Instruments Nanoscope. If the z scale of an AFM image is labelled as 'phase' then the image is identified as an MFM image. The full set of image parameters, stored in the header of the image file, can be displayed using the 'Dump All Parameters' menu item in the Parameters submenu of the STM menu.	•	Image SXM can now read image files produced by the TopoMetrix range of STMs and AFMs.	•	A new SXM menu has been added alongside the SEM and STM menus. The SXM menu contains various items that have been moved from the other menus as they can be applied to SEM, STM, SAM, AFM and MFM images. A new 'SXM Options...' menu item allows the user to specify that images larger or smaller than specified limits will be reduced or magnified automatically after loading. This can include PICT and TIFF images.	•	Multiple images can now be loaded as a stack rather than separate windows, determined by the settings of check boxes in the STM, SAM and SFM Options dialog boxes. The check box in the STM Options dialog box affects only dual images from the Omicron STM. The check box in the SAM Options dialog box is only active if the 'Display PEAK, BGND and RESULT images' check box is selected. The check box in the SFM Options dialog box affects only AFM/MFM images from the Digital Instruments Nanoscope.	•	A new 'FFT Options...' menu item has been added to the FFT submenu of the Process menu (the FFT menu was moved from the menu bar as space was tight on small monitors). This handles the selection of the maximum image size that can be FFT'd - either 256x256 or 512x512. Images can be masked automatically before an FFT is calculated and unmasked after an inverse FFT.	•	A new 'Region Of Interest' item has been added to the 'Propagate' sub-menu in the Options menu. This copies the region of interest (usually a rectangle or line selection) to all other open windows. This is particularly useful when a number of images cover exactly the same spatial region of a sample (eg, SAM images).Bug fixes:	•	The 'Z' cursor (see v1.58 ∑2) is now only displayed when either the selection tool or the magnifying glass are selected. The zoom feature is only available when one of these tools is selected and so displaying the 'Z' cursor when other tools are selected is confusing.	•	For WA Technology STM images tilt compensation did not display the correct z scale calibration. This was due to the way that the calibration information is stored in the file header. This has been fixed. Images that had been 'normalised' by the WA Technology software to use the full ± 32768 range of z values would not load with tilt compensation. These images will now load, but the z scale parameter held in the file header is not the correct value for the image and so the z values are displayed incorrectly.Other changes:	•	In the PowerMac version of Image SXM the Tool window is now displayed in greyscale (or as close to greyscale as is possible for any particular LUT). If the tools become difficult to see when the brightness or contrast controls have been adjusted, click in the Tool window, in the title bar of an image window or option-click in the Info window to restore the original Tool palette.	•	The title bars of SAM image windows now display the filenames in the format 'folder/filename' as the filenames alone convey little useful information regarding their origin.	•	A colour palette named 'Mandelbrot' has been added to the 'Color Tables' submenu in the Options menu.____________________________________________________________________________________v1.58    ∑2    ( 14 Aug 95 )Added features:	•	Image SXM can now read image files in the new Omicron STM format. STS data will follow.Bug fixes:	•	The option to display STM image dimensions in Å rather than nm now works (previously, all STM images used Å as the default unit and so conversion from Å to nm was implemented, but not nm to Å).Other changes:	•	A warning dialog is produced if the user FFTs an image that is not an integer power of two in size.	•	An image that has been masked, FFT'd and ReFFT'd can now have the mask removed. If this is done, then pixel values close to the edge of the image are unreliable. Use with caution.	•	The use of the modifier keys (Option, Shift, Control) when the selection tool (the default crosshair cursor) is active has been changed to make them consistent with NIH Image: Shift is used to constrain a dragged rectangle to be square; Option is used to subtract a new selection from an existing selection; Control is used to add a new selection to an existing selection. Creating a zoom window is now achieved by selecting the Tab key (previously the Option key) and clicking in the image. The cursor changes to a 'Z' when the Tab key is pressed to remind the user of its action. If the Shift key is pressed as well, then the cursor becomes a larger 'Z' to indicate the higher zoom magnification. Selecting the largest square that is an integer power of two in size is now achieved from the first item in the FFT menu (previously the Control key).	•	Animating stacks now updates the window title bar if the frame rates is below 10 frames per second. At higher rates it remains frozen at its initial setting.	•	Text files are displayed in Monaco by default (previously Geneva). This makes some files easier to read, such as the new format Omicron STM parameter files.____________________________________________________________________________________v1.58    ∑1    ( 7 Aug 95 )    General releaseFunctionally identical to v1.58  ß4.____________________________________________________________________________________v1.58    ß4    ( 12 Jul 95 )    Beta releaseAdded features:	•	None.Bug fixes:  •	WA Technology STM images are now flipped vertically to give the correct orientation.  •	The x and y calibrations of WA Tech STM images would appear negative for images greater than 32 nm due to a 16-bit integer overflow (32768 pm = 32 nm). This has been fixed using a 32-bit longint.Other changes:	•	None.____________________________________________________________________________________v1.58    ß3    ( 10 Jul 95 )    Beta releaseAdded features:	•	Image SXM can now read image files produced by the WA Technology STM. The small images that are a part of the image header are not used when browsing for the sake of compatibility with other formats.Bug fixes:  •	The 'Apply LUT' command would produce a dialog box and remove the density (z) calibration of STM images. This was a new feature in NIH Image v1.58 and has now been removed as it is not required - Image SXM compensates for changes in the LUT when calculating z values.  •	The 'Plot Profile' command didn't display the plots correctly if the 'Fixed Y-Axis Scale' preference was checked. The axes and tick marks are now calculated correctly for fixed scale plots.  •	As in earlier versions of Image SXM, the Cmd-R keyboard shortcut is assigned to the 'ReCompensate' menu item, but in v1.58 this key had not been removed from the menu item assigned by NIH Image - 'Rescale/Revert To Saved' in the File menu. This has been fixed.	•	The maximum image width of 4096 pixels on Power Macs gave problems when the total RAM was 16 Mb or less. The maximum width has been reduced to 3072 (as for non-Power Macs) until the bug is traced. Other changes:	•	Cmd-Option-O is a shortcut for selecting the 'SXM Preferences...' menu item.  •  One of the menu items in the Files submenu of the STM menu has become two: 'Browse Images...' has been renamed 'Browse Omicron...' to make it clear that this browsing option expects to find files named according to the Omicron convention, and a new 'Browse Images...' item allows browsing of any other SXM, PICT or TIFF file.____________________________________________________________________________________v1.58    ß2    ( 6 Jul 95 )    Beta releaseAdded features:	•	Cmd-Option-I is a shortcut for executing the 'Invert LUT' and 'Apply LUT' operations in sequence.Bug fixes:	•	As in earlier versions of Image SXM, the Cmd-B and Cmd-F keyboard shortcuts are assigned to the 'Browse Images...' and 'Do FFT' menu items, but in v1.58 these keys had not been removed from the menu items assigned by NIH Image - 'Draw Boundary' and 'Find...' or 'Fill' in the Edit menu. This has been fixed.Other changes:	•	The maximum image width has been increased to 3072 (non-Power Macs) or 4096 pixels (Power Macs). 	•	The need for separate copies of the three SXM variants - SEM, STM and SAM - has been removed now that the application name determines not only the appearance of the splash screen and the assignment of keyboard shortcuts, but also the application icon.  If the icon is not appropriate for the variant running, then when the application quits the user is given the option of changing the icon. The desktop will need to be rebuilt to see the new icon.____________________________________________________________________________________v1.58    ß1    ( 3 Jul 95 )    Beta releaseAdded features:	•	None.Bug fixes:	•	Fixed a bug that caused Image SXM to quit if a zoom window was created, the original image window closed and then the zoom window selected again by clicking in the window rather than on the title bar.	•	If the image window was small, a zoom window could be positioned partially offscreen. This has been fixed. Other changes:	•	Printer halftoning options are now accessible from the 'SXM Preferences...' menu item. ____________________________________________________________________________________v1.58    alpha    ( 2 Jul 95 )    Development versionAdded features:	•	None.Bug fixes:	•	NIH Image v1.58 fixes a number of bugs present in v1.57. See the NIH Image documentation for details.Other changes:	•	Combining the source code for NIH Image v1.58 with that written for Image SXM v1.57 involves a large amount of editing - Image SXM is now a total of 60 000 lines of code. Some coding errors are inevitable. This version is labelled a 'beta' version until it has been checked more thoroughly on other Macs.	•	There is an incompatibility between the image file headers used by NIH Image v1.58 and the file headers used by Image SXM v1.57. The problem only exists for stacks (ie, collections of images or slices saved as a single file). Stacks that are saved using NIH Image v1.58 can be opened by Image SXM but will have one of the file parameters read incorrectly. If this is a particular problem for some users, then let me know - otherwise I will not attempt to recode Image SXM to get around the problem.____________________________________________________________________________________